            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0562" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg468"/>

                <head>No. 316.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 30, 1887</date>.
                        (Received April 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 478.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch numbered 475, of
                    March 26 I have the honor to inclose herewith the copy of a note which I
                    received yesterday from the Marquis of Salisbury, adding a clause to the
                    observations on Article III of your proposal for a <hi rendition="#italic">modus
                        vivendi</hi>, which formed a part of inclosure No. 2 to his lordship’s note
                    of the 24th instant, in reference to the Canadian fisheries.</p>
                <p>I have the honor also to inclose herewith four copies of the note in question,
                    corrected as above, and I beg to add that I have marked the newly inserted
                    clause at page No. 10 of the same.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White</hi>.</signed></closer>





